  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 105 AM MST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nTuesday - Sunday: For the long term period, active weather continues \nfor south central and southeastern Colorado. For Tuesday, overall \nquiet and dry weather is anticipated as the Sunday-Monday storm \nsystem pushes out of the region. The exception to this will be early \nin the day as gusty northerly winds remain in place early across the \nplains, along with isolated light rain showers. Past that, \nadditional troughs may impact the region, particularly Wednesday - \nearly Thursday and Saturday - Sunday, bringing with them increased \nprecipitation chances and breezier conditions. Outside all of that, \nstable and near seasonal temperatures can be anticipated, with \nperiods of mostly clear to partly cloudy skies, with skies cloudiest \nas the waves pass over/near.",
